# Every Engine v2 program on a machine shared with today's system (Engine v2 O17, #2810): the worlds (worldd@), the
# gateways, the directory and the origin. Each world has its own MemoryMax (worldd@'s 2 GB, or its limits.conf from
# world-limits.json: Eden 4 GB), so a world that overruns is ended alone and restarted alone. The slice's own cap is a
# backstop sized so it is never what ends a world: on 24 Nov a 3 GB slice cap ended Eden when a fourth world started.
# Sizing (production host, 24 Nov, measured): 30.6 GiB; today's system peaked at 14.2 GiB in 23 days (its own cap is
# 24 GB, docs/operations.md); 2 GiB for the OS, Caddy and the rest leaves 14 GiB. On the new engine Eden peaks at
# 1.7 GB and a small world at 0.85 GB; eleven worlds (Eden and ten others) at those peaks are 10.2 GB, the gateways,
# directory and origin about 0.1 GB, so 14 GB is that with 40 % to spare, and Eden at its 4 GB cap with the ten others
# at their peaks (12.6 GB) still fits. Raised to 18 GB on 24 Nov (Gene's choice): the eleven worlds, idle, already held
# 10.4 GB, 74 % of 14, too little room for the limits run (limits-run.md), and 20 GB of the machine was free. Both caps
# full at once (18 + today's 14.2 GiB peak) would pass the machine; that is now the margin, not the cap.
# MemoryLow is Eden's (2 GB): a child's MemoryLow only counts up to its parent's.
# The processor and the disk are shared, never capped: at weight 20 against the default 100 the new system gets a
# fifth of what today's gets when both are busy, and all of it when today's is idle, so neither system's world time is
# throttled. Applied live, restarting nothing: memory-bounds.sh.
[Unit]
Description=Souls Engine v2 programs

[Slice]
MemoryMax=18G
MemoryLow=2G
MemorySwapMax=0
CPUWeight=20
IOWeight=20
TasksMax=4096
